=== pnpm ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
These are common pnpm commands used in various situations, use 'pnpm help
-a' to list all commands

Version 11.22.0


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  pnpm [command] [flags]
  pnpm [ -h | --help | -v | --version ]


FLAGS (5) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-r, --recursive  Run the command for each project in the workspace.
-h
    --help
-v
    --version

=== pnpm add ===
Installs a package and any packages that it depends on. By default, any new
package is installed as a prod dependency

=== pnpm install ===
Install all dependencies for a project
alias: i

=== pnpm link ===
Connect the local project to another one
alias: ln

=== pnpm remove ===
Removes packages from node_modules and from the project's package.json
alias: rm

=== pnpm unlink ===
Unlinks a package. Like yarn unlink but pnpm re-installs the dependency
after removing the external link

=== pnpm update ===
Updates packages to their latest version based on the specified range
alias: up

=== pnpm audit ===
Checks for known security issues with the installed packages

=== pnpm list ===
Print all the versions of packages that are installed, as well as their
dependencies, in a tree-structure
alias: ls

=== pnpm outdated ===
Check for outdated packages

=== pnpm why ===
Shows all packages that depend on the specified package

=== pnpm create ===
Create a project from a "create-*" or "@foo/create-*" starter kit

=== pnpm dlx ===
Fetches a package from the registry without installing it as a dependency,
hot loads it, and runs whatever default command binary it exposes

=== pnpm exec ===
Executes a shell command in scope of a project

=== pnpm run ===
Runs a defined package script

=== pnpm config ===
Manage the pnpm configuration files
alias: c

=== pnpm init ===
Create a package.json file

=== pnpm publish ===
Publishes a package to the registry

=== pnpm stage ===
Stage packages for publishing

=== pnpm clean ===
Safely remove node_modules directories from all workspace projects

=== pnpm dedupe ===
Perform an install removing older dependencies in the lockfile if a newer
version can be used

=== pnpm fetch ===
Fetch packages from a lockfile into virtual store, package manifest is
ignored

=== pnpm import ===
Generates a pnpm-lock.yaml from an npm package-lock.json (or
npm-shrinkwrap.json) file

=== pnpm install-test ===
Runs a pnpm install followed immediately by a pnpm test
alias: it

=== pnpm prune ===
Removes extraneous packages

=== pnpm rebuild ===
Rebuild a package
alias: rb

=== pnpm patch ===
Prepare a package for patching

=== pnpm patch-commit ===
Generate a patch out of a directory

=== pnpm patch-remove ===
Remove existing patch files

=== pnpm licenses ===
Check licenses in consumed packages

=== pnpm approve-builds ===
Approve dependencies for running scripts during installation

=== pnpm ignored-builds ===
Print the list of packages with blocked build scripts

=== pnpm start ===
Runs an arbitrary command specified in the package's "start" property of its
"scripts" object

=== pnpm test ===
Runs a package's "test" script, if one was provided
alias: t

=== pnpm bin ===
Prints the directory into which the executables of dependencies are linked

=== pnpm deploy ===
Deploy a package from a workspace

=== pnpm pack ===
Create a tarball from a package

=== pnpm root ===
Prints the effective modules directory

=== pnpm env ===
Manage Node.js versions (deprecated, use runtime)

=== pnpm runtime ===
Manage runtimes
alias: rt

=== pnpm self-update ===
Updates pnpm to the latest version

=== pnpm cat-file ===
Prints the contents of a file based on the hash value stored in the index
file

=== pnpm cat-index ===
Prints the index file of a specific package from the store

=== pnpm find-hash ===
Experimental! Lists the packages that include the file with the specified
hash

=== pnpm store ===

=== pnpm store add ===
Adds new packages to the pnpm store directly. Does not modify any projects
or files outside the store

=== pnpm store path ===
Prints the path to the active store directory

=== pnpm store prune ===
Removes unreferenced (extraneous, orphan) packages from the store

=== pnpm store status ===
Checks for modified packages in the store

=== pnpm cache ===

=== pnpm cache delete ===
Experimental! Deletes metadata cache for the specified package(s). Supports
patterns

=== pnpm cache list ===
Experimental! Lists the available packages metadata cache. Supports
filtering by glob

=== pnpm cache list-registries ===
Experimental! Lists all registries that have their metadata cache locally

=== pnpm cache view ===
Experimental! Views information from the specified package's cache
